        ["Rock tower, painted: a slick shaft with a flat dry top and a pointed foot, in a few big leaning planes with the cleavage painted on. One or two real breaks: an opened joint, a leaning slab", "1 to 7.8 m wide, 3 to 14 m tall; tops 1.6 to 3.5 m", "seven, each made for its place: El Filo, La Aguja, the station's tower, La Torre with its needle, the two lone towers, the buttress", "Play space", "new"],
        ["Tower body: the same rock carried on behind and down, as one big form in two or three slanted planes, greyer and cooler, its cleavage painted as thin lines that carry on from the tower's", "2 m wider than its tower, 10 to 20 m tall", "behind every tower, 3 m back, in place of today's flat blue cards. The station tower's body has a shoulder that the vane's mast stands on", "Background", "new"],
